office_search.py reads Excel and Word files straight from disk. Excel and Word never launch, files aren't locked, macros never run, and UNC shares work.

Setup

pip install openpyxl xlrd pandas

Typical runs

python office_search.py "\\server\share\Finance" -r -q "invoice 4471"
python office_search.py C:\Docs -r -q "legal hold" -q "retention" -o hits.xlsx
python office_search.py C:\Docs -r -q "breach" -q "notify" --all --type word

What it covers

Excel (.xlsx, .xlsm, .xls, .csv): reports the exact sheet and cell, for example Invoices!B3. Add --formulas to also search formula text.
Word (.docx): searches body paragraphs, table cells (with table, row and column), headers and footers, footnotes, endnotes, comments, and text boxes.
Options: the same as the log tool:
--regex, -w for whole words, --all to require every term
--since/--until and --type excel|word
-o hits.xlsx to save every hit with its location plus a summary sheet
Problem files: password-protected or corrupt files are reported and skipped instead of crashing the run.

Not covered: legacy .doc files are listed as skipped. If you have a lot of them, I can add an option that converts them through Word in the background.

You now have three tools that share the same options: pdf_search.py, log_search.py, and office_search.py. If you'd rather run one command across PDFs, Office files and logs in the same folder tree, I can merge them into a single tool.
